  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Throw, catch and crawl",
  "description": "Six players stand in a ring about 6 × 6 metres, with six cones around the outside. One player holds the ball and throws it to someone else in the ring, who has to catch it before it touches the ground.\n\nThe thrower then crawls on hands and feet round any cone and back to their place. The catcher throws on to a new teammate. Call their name before you throw so they are ready.\n\nEasier: throw with a bounce. Harder: two balls at once, or throw a little higher and to the side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Watch the ball all the way into your hands."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Hands in front of your body, fingers spread and thumbs close together."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Throw so your teammate can catch it – gently and at the chest."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
